meta {
  name: Create post with assets
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/media/upload
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Mural en la ciudad",
    "description": "Registro de la sesión",
    "category": "Graffiti",
    "hashtags": [
      "graffiti",
      "guatemala"
    ],
    "assets": [
      {
        "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
        "publicId": "archive-media/photos/uuid",
        "type": "image",
        "isCover": true,
        "thumbnailUrl": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status >= 200 && res.status < 300 && res.body?.id) {
    bru.setVar("postId", res.body.id);
  }
  if (res.status === 201 && res.body?.mediaAssets?.[0]?.id) {
    bru.setVar("assetId", res.body.mediaAssets[0].id);
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  # Create post with assets

  `POST /api/media/upload`

  Register JSON metadata for files already uploaded to storage.

  ## Authentication

  Admin or Editor; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  No path or query parameters.

  ## Request body

  | Field | Type | Rules / default |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | title | string | Required and nonempty. |
  | description | string or null | Optional. |
  | category | string | General if omitted or blank. |
  | hashtags | string[] or null | Defaults to []; send lowercase tags for reliable filtering. |

  | Field | Type | Rules / default |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | assets | object[] | At least one asset required. |
  | assets[].url | string | Required; URL of a previously uploaded file. |
  | assets[].publicId | string | Required; container/blob path returned by Azure authorization. |
  | assets[].type | string | Defaults to image; video (case-insensitive) creates a video, other nonempty values create an image. |
  | assets[].isCover | boolean | false; no unique-cover constraint. |
  | assets[].thumbnailUrl | string or null | Optional thumbnail or video poster URL. |

  Send Content-Type: application/json.

  ```json
  {
    "title": "Mural en la ciudad",
    "description": "Registro de la sesión",
    "category": "Graffiti",
    "hashtags": [
      "graffiti",
      "guatemala"
    ],
    "assets": [
      {
        "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
        "publicId": "archive-media/photos/uuid",
        "type": "image",
        "isCover": true,
        "thumbnailUrl": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Response

  HTTP **201**.

  ```json
  {
    "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
    "title": "City mural",
    "description": "Session documentation",
    "category": "Graffiti",
    "hashtags": [
      "graffiti"
    ],
    "media": [
      {
        "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
        "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
        "type": "image",
        "isCover": true,
        "thumbnailUrl": null
      }
    ],
    "isArchived": false,
    "createdAt": "2026-11-14T12:00:00Z",
    "mediaAssets": [
      {
        "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
        "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
        "type": "image",
        "isCover": true,
        "thumbnailUrl": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 400: At least one asset is required. or model validation.
  - 401: missing, invalid, or expired Bearer token.
  - 403: authenticated token with an insufficient role.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  Does not upload file bytes or verify that URLs exist. Replace sample asset URLs/publicIds with actual upload results. Captures postId and the first assetId. Returns a Location header for the created post.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
